IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp4-childrens-benefits`

-- Tests of section 59 (disabled contributor's child's benefit and orphan's benefit). Every expected value is
-- worked out by hand from the text, as written beside the assertion. The Pension Index is invented.

§ `Tests -- section 59`

§§ `Fixtures`

-- A short Pension Index series, positionally 1986 to 1994: 100 for 1986 to 1991, then 102 (1992), 105 (1993), 105 (1994).
`the test series` MEANS LIST 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 102, 105, 105

§§ `Section 59(1) -- the basic monthly amount`

-- (a): 1991 is $113.14, whatever the index.
#ASSERT `s 59(1) — the basic monthly amount of a disabled contributor's child's benefit or an orphan's benefit` 1991 `the test series` EQUALS JUST 113.14
-- (b): 1992 is 113.14 times the ratio of the Pension Index for 1992 to that for 1991 (102/100), plus $35:
-- 113.14 x 1.02 + 35 = 115.4028 + 35 = 150.4028.
#ASSERT `s 59(1) — the basic monthly amount of a disabled contributor's child's benefit or an orphan's benefit` 1992 `the test series` EQUALS JUST 150.4028
-- (c): 1993 is the 1992 amount times 105/102: 150.4028 x 105/102.
#ASSERT `s 59(1) — the basic monthly amount of a disabled contributor's child's benefit or an orphan's benefit` 1993 `the test series` EQUALS JUST (150.4028 TIMES 105 DIVIDED BY 102)
-- 1994: the 1993 amount times 105/105, the same.
#ASSERT `s 59(1) — the basic monthly amount of a disabled contributor's child's benefit or an orphan's benefit` 1994 `the test series` EQUALS JUST (150.4028 TIMES 105 DIVIDED BY 102)
-- Before 1991 the text gives no amount; a year the series does not reach is not decided either.
#ASSERT `s 59(1) — the basic monthly amount of a disabled contributor's child's benefit or an orphan's benefit` 1990 `the test series` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 59(1) — the basic monthly amount of a disabled contributor's child's benefit or an orphan's benefit` 1995 `the test series` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 59(2) -- a dependent child in part-time attendance`

-- 50% of the amount under paragraph (1)(c): for 1993, 50% x 150.4028 x 105/102.
#ASSERT `s 59(2) — the basic monthly amount for a dependent child in part-time attendance at a school or university` 1993 `the test series` EQUALS JUST (0.5 TIMES 150.4028 TIMES 105 DIVIDED BY 102)
-- Paragraph (1)(c) begins in 1993, so there is no amount "otherwise calculated under paragraph (1)(c)" for 1992.
#ASSERT `s 59(2) — the basic monthly amount for a dependent child in part-time attendance at a school or university` 1992 `the test series` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 59(2) — the basic monthly amount for a dependent child in part-time attendance at a school or university` 1995 `the test series` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 59 -- which subsection governs`

#ASSERT `s 59 — the basic monthly amount of the benefit for the child` FALSE 1993 `the test series` EQUALS JUST (150.4028 TIMES 105 DIVIDED BY 102)
#ASSERT `s 59 — the basic monthly amount of the benefit for the child` TRUE 1993 `the test series` EQUALS JUST (0.5 TIMES 150.4028 TIMES 105 DIVIDED BY 102)
